-- M3 Stage B, Gate B item (iii) fixture: a Div-headed def built
-- from a deliberately expensive prim. `tot check` must never force
-- this body: since the M3 fixes (A1, 2026-09-01) check mode builds
-- NO runtime environment for the user file at all (surface/run.ml
-- skips Interp.define entirely when exec is false), subsuming the
-- older Stage B rule that keyed deferral on the def's Div/IO type
-- head; the head-keyed deferral governs RUN mode only now (see
-- dev/M3-BUILD-LOG.md "Stage B" and SPEC.md section 2, M3 fixes
-- stage A). Were the rule to regress,
-- stringContains below would scan a three-million-character
-- haystack against a five-thousand-one-character needle that
-- never matches (worst case for every scan position: O(hlen *
-- nlen) byte comparisons and allocations), which is roughly a
-- minute of real work (empirically ~66s on the build machine);
-- deferred, `tot check` never calls it at all, so this file's own
-- check time stays a small fraction of a second (mostly lexing
-- the two literals below). Assert a COARSE wall-clock bound
-- only: this pins the deferred rule, not performance tuning.
def haystack : String := ""
def needle : String := ""
def slow : Div Bool := pureDiv Bool (stringContains haystack needle)
